<title>USA: St Joseph hogs off $0.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs off $0.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Wednesday, barrows and gilts were $0.50 lower. Top $46.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>Marketings and slaughter under both last week and a year ago but dressed pork trade lower and packers not pushing for hogs. Moved 111,000 Interior Iowa Wednesday and any more that's considered fairly liberal receipts. Beautiful weather and Spring field work under way but very few dirt farmers raise hogs anymore and this will not affect marketings to much extent.</p>
<p>    US 1-3	230-270 lbs    46.00-46.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3	270-290 lbs    44.50-45.50</p>
<p>    US 2-4	290-310 lbs    42.50-43.50</p>
<p>Sows - steady. Top $48.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2	300-450 lbs    43.00</p>
<p>		    450-500 lbs    44.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3	500-550 lbs    46.00</p>
<p>		    550-700 lbs    47.00-48.00</p>
<p>    Boars:	300-700 lbs    39.50</p>
<p>		    200-300 lbs    40.50</p>
</text>
